hub.com/repos/DataDog/dd-trace-go/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DataDog/dd-trace-go/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DataDog/dd-trace-go/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DataDog/dd-trace-go/deployments","created_at":"2016-09-08T07:47:44Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T09:15:12Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-12T10:49:06Z","git_url":"git://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-go.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:DataDog/dd-trace-go.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-go.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-go","homepage":"https://docs.datadoghq.com/tracing/","size":77267,"stargazers_count":813,"watchers_count":813,"language":"Go","has_issues":true,"has_projects":false,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":493,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":190,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["apm","appsec","datadog","distributed-tracing","monitoring","opentelemetry","opentracing","otel","performance","profiling","tracing"],"visibility":"public","forks":493,"open_issues":190,"watchers":813,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"<!--\r\nIf you have identified a specific bug in the dd-trace-go codebase, please describe it here. If the\r\nissue requires debugging or investigation of your specific private setup, that is best accomplished via support. Please contact Datadog [support](http://docs.datadoghq.com/help/).\r\n-->\r\n\r\nHello, I have updated to `go-redis/v9` and CI detected a data race.\r\n\r\n**Version of dd-trace-go**\r\n<!-- If you aren't using the [latest version](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-go/releases) of dd-trace-go, try upgrading first to see if your issue has already been resolved -->\r\nv1.58.0\r\n\r\n**Describe what happened:**\r\n<!-- Is the issue for a specific `contrib/` package? -->\r\nA data race condition was detected when using `dd-trace-go` with the `go-redis/v9` package. This involves concurrent read and write operations in the datadogHook and internal pool methods of `go-redis/v9`. The race condition occurs during the execution of WrapClient or NewClient methods from `dd-trace-go/v1/contrib/redis/go-redis.v9`.\r\n\r\n**Describe what you expected:**\r\nThe expected behavior is the safe and race-condition-free execution of `dd-trace-go` methods when interfacing with `go-redis/v9`, ensuring thread safety and data integrity.\r\n\r\n**Steps to reproduce the issue:**\r\n<!-- If you can include a minimal code sample to reproduce the issue it can significantly reduce resolution time -->\r\n\r\n- source code\r\n```go\r\nfunc main() {\r\n\tctx := context.Background()\r\n\topts, err := getOpts()\r\n\tif err != nil {\r\n\t\tpanic(err)\r\n\t}\r\n\tclient := redistrace.NewClient(opts, redistrace.WithAnalytics(true), redistrace.WithServiceName(\"redis\"))\r\n\r\n\tclient.Set(ctx, \"key\", \"value\", 0)\r\n\r\n\tvar check string\r\n\tif err := client.Get(ctx, \"key\").Scan(&check); err != nil {\r\n\t\tpanic(err)\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tfmt.Println(\"check:\", check)\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunc getOpts() (*redis.Options, error) {\r\n\tredisURL := envutil.GetString(\"REDIS_URL\", \"redis://localhost:6379\")\r\n\topts, err := redis.ParseURL(redisURL)\r\n\tif err != nil {\r\n\t\treturn nil, err\r\n\t}\r\n\topts.MaxRetries = envutil.GetInt(\"REDIS_MAX_RETRIES\", 1)\r\n\topts.PoolSize = envutil.GetInt(\"REDIS_POOL_SIZE\", 10*runtime.NumCPU())\r\n\topts.MinIdleConns = envutil.GetInt(\"REDIS_MIN_IDLE_CONNS\", runtime.NumCPU())\r\n\topts.ConnMaxLifetime = envutil.GetDuration(\"REDIS_MAX_CONN_AGE\", 30*time.Minute)\r\n\topts.ReadTimeout = envutil.GetDuration(\"REDIS_READ_TIMEOUT\", 2*time.Second)\r\n\topts.WriteTimeout = envutil.GetDuration(\"REDIS_WRITE_TIMEOUT\", 3*time.Second)\r\n\topts.PoolTimeout = envutil.GetDuration(\"REDIS_POOL_TIMEOUT\", 5*time.Second)\r\n\treturn opts, nil\r\n}\r\n```\r\n- run cmd\r\n```\r\ngo run -race main.go \r\n```\r\n- found 10 data races (only one is listed)\r\n```\r\n==================\r\nWARNING: DATA RACE\r\nRead at 0x00c00011cd20 by goroutine 12:\r\n  runtime.slicecopy()\r\n      /usr/local/opt/go/libexec/src/runtime/slice.go:310 +0x0\r\n  gopkg.in/DataDog/dd-trace-go.v1/contrib/redis/go-redis%2ev9.(*datadogHook).DialHook.func1()\r\n      /Users/ryo/go/pkg/mod/gopkg.in/!data!dog/dd-trace-go.v1@v1.58.0/contrib/redis/go-redis.v9/redis.go:118 +0x339\r\n  github.com/redis/go-redis/v9.(*hooksMixin).dialHook()\r\n      /Users/ryo/go/pkg/mod/github.com/redis/go-redis/v9@v9.3.0/redis.go:168 +0xb0\r\n  github.com/redis/go-redis/v9.(*hooksMixin).dialHook-fm()\r\n      <autogenerated>:1 +0x29\r\n  github.com/redis/go-redis/v9.newConnPool.func1()\r\n      /Users/ryo/go/pkg/mod/github.com/redis/go-redis/v9@v9.3.0/options.go:504 +0xa4\r\n  github.com/redis/go-redis/v9/internal/pool.(*ConnPool).dialConn()\r\n      /Users/ryo/go/pkg/mod/github.com/redis/go-redis/v9@v9.3.0/internal/pool/pool.go:205 +0x186\r\n  github.com/redis/go-redis/v9/internal/pool.(*ConnPool).addIdleConn()\r\n      /Users/ryo/go/pkg/mod/github.com/redis/go-redis/v9@v9.3.0/internal/pool/pool.go:143 +0x6f\r\n  github.com/redis/go-redis/v9/internal/pool.(*ConnPool).checkMinIdleConns.func1()\r\n      /Users/ryo/go/pkg/mod/github.com/redis/go-redis/v9@v9.3.0/internal/pool/pool.go:126 +0x34\r\n\r\nPrevious write at 0x00c00011cd20 by main goroutine:\r\n  gopkg.in/DataDog/dd-trace-go.v1/contrib/redis/go-redis%2ev9.additionalTagOptions()\r\n      /Users/ryo/go/pkg/mod/gopkg.in/!data!dog/dd-trace-go.v1@v1.58.0/contrib/redis/go-redis.v9/redis.go:104 +0xe35\r\n  gopkg.in/DataDog/dd-trace-go.v1/contrib/redis/go-redis%2ev9.WrapClient()\r\n      /Users/ryo/go/pkg/mod/gopkg.in/!data!dog/dd-trace